Task: Establish a reproducible render-measurement contract.

Summary:
- Added a pure render-window contract that records post-render triangles/calls, camera focus, zoom, pixel ratio, and shadow-pass settings; reports frame span, peaks, means, and mixed-setting detection.
- Added a dev-only browser probe with named start/stop/snapshot/clear controls and a scene inventory readout, while leaving production behavior free of the probe.
- Extended the render loop with an optional post-render callback so samples represent the current WebGL frame.
- Recorded controlled Chromium baseline windows and the culling finding: zero meshes disable frustum culling, so custom camera filtering was rejected as a likely source of regression without meaningful measured headroom.

